"The strategic form of the signaling game of Figure III. A strategy of A gives the message sent
if of type t1 and if of type t2, so m/m' sends m if t1 and m' if t2; B's strategies are the
responses r1 and r2 to m'. Payoffs are expected payoffs under the prior (t1 0.9, t2 0.1). The
equilibrium in which A sends m regardless of type and B responds with r1 is the profile (m/m, r1)."

